    "drs_lead": "Passing door selection in Milan during the 2026/2027 clubbing season depends on matching your outfit, footwear, group balance and arrival time to three distinct venue tiers rather than relying on generic nightlife myths. Tier 3 luxury rooms - Armani Privé (Via Gastone Pisoni 1), Just Me Milano beneath Torre Branca (ex Just Cavalli, open 7 nights a week), 20th-floor Voya Rooftop (Viale Achille Papa 30), Terrazza Duomo 21 and Philipp's Milano - enforce strict sartorial elegance (21+/23+): collared dress shirt, tailored trousers, blazer and leather loafers or derbies for men, evening dress or tailored jumpsuit for women, with zero athletic sneakers, hoodies, shorts or caps.",
    "drs_deep": "Tier 2 dinner-show and commercial flagship clubs - Pineta Milano and The Grace Club (Via Messina 38, M5 Cenisio), 55 Milano (Via Piero della Francesca 55), REPVBLIC (Piazza della Repubblica 12), Il Gattopardo, MIB, Dazi, The Club, Tocqueville 13 and Hollywood - accept clean monochrome dark leather low-tops only when paired with a shirt and jacket, whereas Tier 1 electronic warehouses (Volt, Amnesia, Gate, Tunnel, Super Club Tortona and Magazzini Generali) favour curated monochrome black urban attire. All-male groups of 4+ guests are strongly advised to reserve a 100 percent bottle-credit VIP table (from 250-350 EUR via Concierge WhatsApp +39 351 912 7047 at 0% partner fee).",
