    "mgg_lead": "Founded in 1995 inside an early-20th-century industrial warehouse at Via Pietrasanta 16 (Zona Ripamonti / Porta Romana, 10 minutes from Bocconi University and M3 Lodi TIBB), Magazzini Generali Milano remains one of northern Italy's historic live-concert and late-night club arenas. Its two-level architecture pairs a high-ceilinged main floor with concert stage, full-wall LED visuals and concert-grade sound with an elevated wrap-around mezzanine balcony housing private VIP bottle tables directly above the crowd.",
